Title: Hindenburg’s inauguration
subtitle: We must be prepared for the worst.
view-if: year = 1925 and month = 5 and president == "Hindenburg"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

Paul von Hindenburg has now been inaugurated as President of the Republic, placing many crucial levers of government in the hands of an ardent reactionary. We must wait and see what his first actions shall be.

- @luther: Leading a Right Coalition, Luther finds he has Hindenburg’s full support.
- @marx: Hindenburg pressures Marx into allowing the DNVP into the Coalition.
- @gessler: Hindenburg sacks Gessler!
- @stresemann: With Hindenburg’s express approval, Stresemann expels us from the Coalition in favor of the DNVP.

@luther
view-if: chancellor == "Luther"

Leading a Right Coalition, Luther finds he has Hindenburg’s full support. 

@marx
view-if: chancellor == "Marx"
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 0; dnvp_in_government = 1; right_coalition = 1

Hindenburg pressures Marx into allowing the DNVP into the Coalition.

@gessler
view-if: chancellor == "Gessler"
on-arrival: chancellor = "Marx"; chancellor_party = "Z"; dnvp_in_government = 1; spd_toleration = 0; right_coalition = 1

Hindenburg sacks Gessler, viewing him as too liberal. To succeed Gessler, Hindenburg re-appoints Wilhelm Marx at the head of a Right Coalition including the DNVP.

@stresemann
view-if: chancellor == "Stresemann"
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 0; dnvp_in_government = 0; right_coalition = 1; grand_coalition = 0

With Hindenburg’s express approval, Stresemann expels us from the Coalition in favor of the DNVP. Our party is outraged, but there is little we can do.
